# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Multi-GB artifacts. None of these are source: every one is regenerated by a
# script in this repo (see README "Reproducing"). GitHub also rejects files
# over 100 MB, so committing them is not merely undesirable, it fails.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore only treats '#' as a comment at the START of a line. An
# inline "# ..." after a pattern becomes part of the pattern and silently
# matches nothing — which is how a 17 GB `git add` happens.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# K9 model containers (1.1 GB .. 3.8 GB each)
*.k9
# per-tensor digit/scale dumps from the earlier experiments
*.npz
*.npy
# QLoRA adapters (~71 MB) and merged models (2.9 GB)
*.safetensors
*.gz
# the compiled rANS coder; build it with experiments/rans_fast.py
*.so
results/printed_model.txt
results/*.log

# caches and environments
# 31 GB of downloaded model weights
.hf-cache/
# bitsandbytes/peft venv (144 MB)
.venv-baselines/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Phase 2 bulk data: the scraped corpus, per-project reconstructions, and every
# training/eval output. Rebuild with phase2/build_sft.py (see phase2/README.md).
phase2/data/
phase2/out/

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# big llama.cpp fork artifacts (session 24)
results/*.gguf
